# Markdown Viewer 3.11.0

_Released August 3, 2026_

This update makes it easier to understand what changed without leaving your workspace.

## Release notes in your workspace

- Release notes now open automatically in the tab list after Markdown Viewer updates to a new version.
- The note opens once per version. Close its tab after reading it and it stays dismissed until the next update.
- The release-note tab is read only, uses Markdown Viewer's app logo, and behaves like a temporary file without being added to Explorer or saved with your documents.

## Easier to find again

- **About Markdown Viewer** now includes **Show Release Notes**, which reopens the current version's note in the tab list at any time.
- The bundled `RELEASE_NOTES` document has no file extension and remains available offline in the web, PWA, and desktop builds.

## Consistent versioning

- The web app, offline cache, and Neutralino desktop packages now report version **3.11.0**.
- Release-note visibility is tracked locally per version and does not require an account or network request.

For the complete project history, see the [changelog](https://github.com/ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).
